{"text": "Looking at this problem, I need to find C(53,13) and then sum its decimal digits.\n\n## Calculating C(53,13)\n\nI'll use the iterative formula approach to avoid overflow and ensure exact calculation:\n\nFor C(n,k), I can compute: result = 1, then iterate i from 1 to k with:\nresult = result \u00d7 (n - i + 1) / i\n\nLet me trace through this step-by-step:\n\n**Steps 1-3:**\n- i=1: (1 \u00d7 53) / 1 = 53\n- i=2: (53 \u00d7 52) / 2 = 2,756 / 2 = 1,378\n- i=3: (1,378 \u00d7 51) / 3 = 70,278 / 3 = 23,426\n\n**Steps 4-6:**\n- i=4: (23,426 \u00d7 50) / 4 = 1,171,300 / 4 = 292,825\n- i=5: (292,825 \u00d7 49) / 5 = 14,348,425 / 5 = 2,869,685\n- i=6: (2,869,685 \u00d7 48) / 6 = 137,744,880 / 6 = 22,957,480\n\n**Steps 7-9:**\n- i=7: (22,957,480 \u00d7 47) / 7 = 1,079,001,560 / 7 = 154,143,080\n- i=8: (154,143,080 \u00d7 46) / 8 = 7,090,501,680 / 8 = 886,322,710\n- i=9: (886,322,710 \u00d7 45) / 9 = 39,884,521,950 / 9 = 4,431,613,550\n\n**Steps 10-12:**\n- i=10: (4,431,613,550 \u00d7 44) / 10 = 194,990,996,200 / 10 = 19,499,099,620\n- i=11: (19,499,099,620 \u00d7 43) / 11 = 838,461,283,660 / 11 = 76,223,753,060\n- i=12: (76,223,753,060 \u00d7 42) / 12 = 3,201,397,628,520 / 12 = 266,783,135,710\n- i=13: (266,783,135,710 \u00d7 41) / 13 = 10,938,108,564,110 / 13 = **841,392,966,470**\n\n## Verification\nLet me verify: 13 \u00d7 841,392,966,470 = 10,938,108,564,110 \u2713\n\n## Summing the Digits\n\nC(53,13) = 841,392,966,470\n\nThe digits are: 8, 4, 1, 3, 9, 2, 9, 6, 6, 4, 7, 0\n\nSum = 8 + 4 + 1 + 3 + 9 + 2 + 9 + 6 + 6 + 4 + 7 + 0\n    = (8 + 4) + (1 + 3 + 9 + 2 + 9) + (6 + 6 + 4 + 7) + 0\n    = 12 + 24 + 23\n    = **59**\n\nANSWER: 59", "usage": {"calls": 1, "input_tokens": 946, "output_tokens": 12867, "cost_usd": 0.065281, "latency_s": 97.77157521247864}, "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "stop_reason": "end_turn"}